func groupByDay(
    _ dates: [Date],
    calendar: Calendar = .current
) -> [Date: [Date]] {
    Dictionary(grouping: dates) { date in
        calendar.startOfDay(for: date)
    }
}
```

`Dictionary(grouping:)` collects dates with the same key into an array. Using `calendar.startOfDay(for:)` as that key groups all dates belonging to the same calendar day, regardless of their time.

The supplied calendar determines day boundaries, including its time zone and daylight-saving rules. It defaults to the user’s current calendar; pass a configured calendar when you need a specific time zone. Dictionary keys are unordered, so sort them if you need chronological display.
